# asArray call-relationship walkthrough

I originally started documenting this trail from `js/view/Properties.js`. The asArray in the title was a term left over from a search at the time, not a name in the imports at the top of the file; I initially treated it as a possible lead to follow up near the properties UI, without recording the relationship as an established conclusion.

The top of the file confirms three direct dependencies:

```js
import {h} from "inferno-hyperscript";
import {VirtualDOMView} from "./VirtualDOMView";
import {getLanguages} from "./languages";
```

The tentative reading order is to first look at the expressions where `h` appears, then go back to where `VirtualDOMView` is used, and finally check which UI construction branch `getLanguages` is passed to. `languages` and asArray turned up in the same search, but that isn't grounds to record a direct call.

The assessment in the first draft was that the relationship involving asArray could probably be worked out by following the imports within Properties. This hasn't been checked section by section yet; in particular, there is no record of the actual arguments, return value, or the node that receives it.

# HTML Descriptor Creation Migration Notes

In the earlier investigation, after seeing an issue name related to HTML descriptors, we first went to `internal/sozi-desktop` at revision `v_prev` and opened `js/Storage.js`. The search terms used at the time were `controller`, `storage`, `html`, `createhtmlfile`, `descriptor`, and `save`.

The file header listed these direct dependencies:

```js
import {SVGDocumentWrapper} from "./svg/SVGDocumentWrapper";
import {backendList} from "./backend/AbstractBackend";
import {EventEmitter} from "events";
import nunjucks from "nunjucks";
```

The first draft treated Storage as the main entry point for HTML Descriptor Creation. The plan was to continue tracing through Controller, the save action, and the descriptor object. This assessment was not backed by a complete call chain, but no other file location had been recorded at the time.

For the migration, first pin `v_prev`, then start at `js/Storage.js` and check the adjacency between `descriptor` and `save`. If all you can see is the file-header dependencies or the entry point from Controller into Storage, stop at the last confirmed object. Details of the new path, actual creation function, caller, and return-value handoff have not been filled in.

